---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="About"
	description="How Ricardo Yanez approaches software engineering, architecture, and engineering leadership."
>
	<section class="page-section">
		<div class="container">
			<p class="eyebrow">About</p>
			<h1>I never really stopped being a software engineer.</h1>
			<p class="lede">
				My responsibilities grew from implementing software to shaping systems, technical direction,
				and engineering work. The hands-on part never disappeared.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="path-title">
		<div class="container">
			<h2 id="path-title">A widening scope</h2>
			<ol class="career-path">
				<li><span>Software Engineer</span></li>
				<li><span>Senior Software Engineer</span></li>
				<li><span>Software Architect</span></li>
				<li><span>Lead Software Engineer</span></li>
			</ol>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="practice-title">
		<div class="container two-column">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">The work today</p>
				<h2 id="practice-title">What changed, and what did not.</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="content">
				<p>
					Over time, I took on more responsibility for architecture, technical decisions, system
					design, mentoring, development coordination, infrastructure, and operation.
				</p>
				<p>
					I still write and review code, investigate failures, design solutions, and build proofs of
					concept. Staying close to implementation keeps my decisions tied to the system the team
					actually has to maintain.
				</p>
				<p>
					I am most interested in the decisions that survive contact with production: clear
					boundaries, explicit trade-offs, useful diagnostics, and changes that another engineer can
					understand later.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="background-title">
		<div class="container two-column">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">Background</p>
				<h2 id="background-title">From legacy systems to cloud platforms.</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="content">
				<p>
					I have been building software since 2006. I started with desktop and business systems in
					Venezuela, later worked remotely with teams in Costa Rica, and continued my career in
					Chile.
				</p>
				<p>
					That path has taken me through legacy migrations, financial software, integrations,
					distributed workflows, cloud infrastructure, and engineering leadership. It is why I care
					as much about changing a system safely as I do about designing the next one.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	h1 {
		max-width: 13ch;
	}

	.career-path {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
		margin: 3rem 0 0;
		padding: 0;
		list-style: none;
		counter-reset: career;
	}

	.career-path li {
		position: relative;
		padding: 3rem 1.25rem 0 0;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
		counter-increment: career;
	}

	.career-path li::before {
		position: absolute;
		top: -0.65rem;
		left: 0;
		padding-right: 0.75rem;
		background: var(--background);
		color: var(--accent);
		content: '0' counter(career);
		font-family: 'SFMono-Regular', Consolas, monospace;
		font-size: 0.8rem;
	}

	.career-path span {
		display: block;
		max-width: 12rem;
		font-weight: 620;
		line-height: 1.35;
	}

	.two-column {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.8fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr);
		gap: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 8rem);
	}

	@media (max-width: 44rem) {
		.career-path {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: 2rem;
		}

		.two-column {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
	}
</style>
